schema: spec-driven

context: |
  Domain: manufacturing operations digitalization (neuwerk, MPEE Operations Digitalization, OD).
  Changes in this folder arrive from OD's Lane 3 front-end (requirements -> tool-decision gate ->
  business case -> handover). OD owns the demand until this team formally accepts it.

  Deployment: containerized apps go to CMO (Kubernetes) with the standard manifests via GitOps.
  Shop-floor data: IIoT Edge Platform -> data platform (Databricks, Azure Storage Account, Parquet).
  Approved OT interfaces: MQTT to the edge platform where applicable; reuse central systems and data
  stores across locations; no new proprietary silo.
  Stack guardrails: ⟨published technology guardrails - IT action item; e.g. Python, FastAPI, SQL⟩
  Language: all artefacts in English.

rules:
  proposal:
    - State bankable impact apart from assumption-dependent benefit
    - Name the route (3a.1 reuse, 3a.2 self-develop, 3a.3 external build, 3a.4 integrate, 3b connector)
  specs:
    - Describe observable behaviour for plant users and downstream systems, not implementation
    - Every requirement that reads or publishes shop-floor data names the data contract it depends on
    - Write growth boundaries as explicit non-goals in design.md, not as requirements
  design:
    - State hosting, interfaces, data model, Cyber Security pattern reused, and who runs it (build-and-run)
  tasks:
    - Include logging and observability, standard manifests, acceptance test, Cyber Security sign-off,
      and the handover checklist before ownership transfers
